-- title:
--   E[p] as truncation of the formal mathcal O_D-module, ramified case
-- statement:
--   Let $q\neq q'$ be primes and $a,b\in\mathbb Q$ be such that `IsIndefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt a b q q'` holds, i.e. $a>0$ or $b>0$ and, for every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$, the completion $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_v$ has all nonzero elements invertible exactly when $v$ contains $q$ or $q'$. Let $\Lambda\subseteq\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ be a $\mathbb Z$-submodule that is a maximal order (it contains $1$, is closed under multiplication, spans the algebra over $\mathbb Q$, is finitely generated, and is maximal among such). Let $p$ be a prime with $p=q$ or $p=q'$, let $k$ be a field of characteristic $p$, let $N\in\mathbb N$, and let $E$ be a fake elliptic curve over $k$ of level $N$ with $\Lambda$-action, in the sense of the structure `FakeEllipticCurve`. Let $H$ be a commutative Hopf $k$-algebra equipped with, for every $k$-algebra $T$, a bijection $e_T$ from `WithConv (H →ₐ[k] T)` (a wrapper on the $k$-algebra homomorphisms $H\to T$) onto the set of $T$-points of $E$ over $\operatorname{Spec} k$ killed by $p$ under the group law `E.L`, these bijections being natural in the sense that for $g':T\to T'$ the scheme morphism underlying $e_{T'}(g'\circ\chi)$ is $\operatorname{Spec} g'$ followed by the morphism underlying $e_T(\chi)$. Then there exist: a coordinate map $\mathrm{coord}\colon\Lambda\to\mathbb W(\mathbb F_{p^2})^2$ satisfying `IsOrderCoord Λ p coord` (additive, sending $1$ to $(1,0)$, multiplicative for the twisted rule involving $p$ and the Witt Frobenius, injective, with dense image, and compatible with reduced traces); a two-dimensional formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $X$ over $k$ with group law $F=X.F$, Witt-vector action and uniformiser series; formal coordinates $\theta$ for $E$ in two variables; a proof that `E.IsFormalModuleVia coord X θ` holds, so that $\theta$ are formal coordinates for `E.L` with law $F$ and the action of $m\in\Lambda$ on $E$ is computed by the series $\mathrm{act}((\mathrm{coord}\,m)_1)+_F\mathrm{act}((\mathrm{coord}\,m)_2)\circ\varpi$; a natural number $\nu$; and a $k$-algebra isomorphism $\Phi$ from $k[[X_1,X_2]]$ modulo the ideal generated by the $p$-th iterate series `X.F.nthSeries p` (the multiplication-by-$p$ series of $F$) onto $H$, with the following two properties. First, for every $k$-algebra $T$ and every $\chi\colon H\to_{\mathrm{alg}} T$, putting $s_i=\chi(\Phi(\overline{X_i}))$: there is an ideal $J\subseteq T$ with $J^{\nu+1}=0$ containing every $s_i$; for every power series $G$ one has $\chi(\Phi(\overline G))=\mathrm{nilEval}\,\nu\,G\,s$, the evaluation at $s$ of the truncation of $G$ in degrees $\le\nu$ in each variable; and the $p$-torsion point $e_T(\chi)$ equals $\theta_T(s)$. Second, conversely, for every $k$-algebra $T$, every ideal $J$ with $J^{n+1}=0$ and every tuple $s\colon\{1,2\}\to J$ with $\mathrm{nilEval}\,n$ of each component of `X.F.nthSeries p` vanishing at $s$, there is a $k$-algebra homomorphism $\chi\colon H\to T$ with $\chi(\Phi(\overline{X_i}))=s_i$ for both $i$.
--
--   This identifies the Hopf algebra representing the $p$-torsion of a fake elliptic curve in characteristic $p$, at a prime $p$ where the quaternion algebra ramifies, with the quotient of $k[[X_1,X_2]]$ by the multiplication-by-$p$ series of the associated formal $\mathcal O_D$-module, by an isomorphism pinned down on points through the given torsion dictionary. It feeds the ramified half of the statement on primitives and the trace of the $\Lambda$-action, `exists_specialFormalODModule_linearMap_primitives_of_ramified`, in the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation of Shimura curves.
